26,2,,status,May,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":2,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
27,2,,status,Rin,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":3,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
28,2,,status,Asuka,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
29,2,,status,Shunichi,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
30,2,1,talk,Rin,,The bin house at the station block smells terrible in summer! And the supervised mornings on the next lane take almost an hour each time.,"{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
31,2,1,talk,Midori,,"A shelter is quite expensive, even with the subsidy. Also, we're spending a lot every year just on nets and deodorants because of the open bags.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
32,2,1,talk,Shunichi,,"People are reluctant to be the ""bin police"" and turn away late bags. Plus, the station block started fighting over maintenance after they built theirs.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
33,2,1,talk,May,,"Those supervised mornings are a real time sink. Also, the truck arrives so early that some of us would have to be up before dawn.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
34,2,1,talk,Asuka,,"The person whose gate the bins are at has complained the most. Also, some of our frontages are way too narrow to fit a bin bay.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
35,2,2,talk,Rin,,"@May, if the truck comes that early, who is going to be awake to watch the bins?","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,2,talk,Midori,,"@Asuka, if some spots are too narrow, does that mean we can't move the bins to everyone's house?","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@Midori, the cost of a shelter seems high, but the current ""open bag"" system is costing us money and causing complaints.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,2,talk,May,,"@Rin, exactly. It's not just the time; it's the timing. It's a lot to ask of people every single week.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Midori, yes. One house has a driveway and another is very narrow. A rotating system might not be physically possible for everyone.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,3,talk,Rin,,"I don't want a smelly box in front of my house! If the bin house is that bad, I'm against a permanent structure.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,3,talk,Midori,,I'm worried about the initial cost of a structure. But the yearly ledger shows we are wasting money on temporary fixes.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,3,talk,Shunichi,,"If we force people to supervise the bins, we'll just end up with more arguments since nobody wants to be the bad guy.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,3,talk,May,,"I agree with Shunichi. The ""supervised"" idea sounds like a recipe for burnout and resentment.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,3,talk,Asuka,,We can't just leave it at the same gate forever. The complaint log proves it's unfair to that one neighbor.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
